  "observations": {
    "weightPrecision": "BuildShrinkAAInfo uses integer0x2000 normalization (13 fractional bits), quotient/remainder carry and low14bit packed weights plus boundary/base+1 flags. For full unclipped rectangles the corroborated reference uses successive floor(cumulative_overlap*8192/source_span) differences; each target sums8192.",
    "oneAxis": "ShrinkDIB_CY retains weighted Q13 channel accumulators and emits clamped signed (6*current-previous-next)>>15, replicating edge accumulator rows. This resolves the52 one-byte differences in the prior floating model. Raw shift and division instructions were independently inspected.",
    "twoShrinkAxes": "SrkYDIB_SrkCX first converts horizontal weighted channels with +0x1000 then >>13. ShrinkDIB_CY_SrkCX accumulates vertical Q13 channels and applies (12*center-left-right-up-down)>>16 with edge replication and saturation. Applying a single floating2D average changes operation order.",
    "sharpen": "Explicit six-argument SharpenInput ABI reviewed from x64 registers/stack. It has separate flags/bypass, three-byte channel guards, 12*center-neighbor integer shift3 and saturation. It must not be conflated with the separate fused13bit shrink paths.",
    "output": "OutputAATo32BPP_RGB writes RGB storage with zero high byte in the inspected path; original vendor32bit alpha OR repair is still a separate later stage.",
    "mixed": "BuildExpandAAInfo uses six-decimal integer kernel construction, calls DivFD6 and RaisePower (argument1414214), then packs13bit coefficients. Mixed shrink/enlarge is a separate path, not a bilinear or nearest fallback. Its exact helper/callback/state behavior remains unresolved.",
    "abi": "Only SharpenInput is explicitly ABI-annotated; twelve other signatures are decompiler-inferred and remain unverified. Arithmetic findings were cross-checked with original instructions and independent native probes. Do not trust guessed struct layouts."
  },
